# Reader Flutter — Multi-Platform Layout

App: `apps/reader_flutter/`. Targets: **iOS**, **Android** (mobile) · **Web** · **macOS**, **Linux**, **Windows** (desktop).

## Directory structure

```
lib/
├── config/          ┐
├── design/          │
├── l10n/            │  COMMON — shared by every platform
├── models/          │  (logic, tokens, routing, strings)
├── providers/       │
├── router/          │
├── storage/         │
├── utils/           │
├── common/platform/ ┘  shell guards (useMobileShell, useWebShell, useDesktopShell)
├── screens/            route adapters — branch only, no platform layout
│
├── mobile/             iOS + Android UI ONLY
│   ├── design/
│   ├── layout/
│   ├── screens/
│   └── widgets/
│       ├── shell/
│       ├── catalog/
│       └── reader/
│
├── web/                Flutter Web UI ONLY
│   ├── design/
│   ├── layout/
│   ├── screens/
│   └── widgets/
│
└── desktop/            macOS + Linux + Windows UI ONLY (one codebase, three runners)
    ├── design/
    ├── layout/
    ├── screens/
    └── widgets/
```

**Migration note:** legacy mobile widgets still live in `lib/widgets/` and mobile branches in `lib/screens/`. New mobile UI goes in `lib/mobile/`. Move files when touching a screen.

## Platform → folder

| Platforms | UI folder | Runners |
| --- | --- | --- |
| iOS, Android | `lib/mobile/` | `ios/`, `android/` |
| Web | `lib/web/` | `web/` |
| macOS, Linux, Windows | `lib/desktop/` | `macos/`, `linux/`, `windows/` |

## Cross-platform rules

1. **Common once** — providers, models, storage, API, l10n, shared design tokens.
2. **UI three times** — implement in `mobile/`, `web/`, and `desktop/` separately.
3. **No cross-imports** between `mobile/`, `web/`, and `desktop/`. Route adapters in `lib/screens/` may import all three.
4. **Share tokens & patterns**, not widget trees or scaffolds.
5. Feature parity across all six targets unless explicitly scoped (e.g. Android `FLAG_SECURE`).

## Feature checklist

1. Logic → common (`providers/`, `storage/`, etc.)
2. Mobile UI → `lib/mobile/screens/` + `lib/mobile/widgets/`
3. Web UI → `lib/web/screens/` + `lib/web/widgets/`
4. Desktop UI → `lib/desktop/screens/` + `lib/desktop/widgets/`
5. Route adapter → `lib/screens/<name>_screen.dart`
6. Strings → `lib/l10n/app_en.arb`, `app_am.arb`
7. Verify → `make reader-run-{android,ios,web,macos,linux,windows}`

See `DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` for shared token details.
